  "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,b\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & 0\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-{b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2}) \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & {b}^{2} \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{b}^{2} \\\\ 2{b}^{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
